n Kobe  Commander hebari Lieutenant Commander  helmeppo and four other members who  haven't been named yet but that can't be  all can it and I'm not talking about  other minor and as of yet unnamed  members I'm talking about the leadership  of Sword there is no way that this  powerful top secret organization was  established by Drake alone a man who is  clearly a field agent he went out on a  dangerous undercover mission for an  extended period of time so he clearly  wasn't the one giving out orders from  headquarters this means that there has  to be someone else who is behind the  establishment of sword and who is in a  position to actually command and  coordinate the operations of the entire  agency in my opinion the top candidates  for being the true leader or leaders of  Sword include kuzan fujitora GARP and  sengoku smoker is also a potential  candidate but he's definitely not my Top  Choice in one of his recent videos  grandline review pointed out that smoker  doesn't seem to know much about kuzan's  movements so it's likely that if smoker  is a member of Sword then koozan isn't  and vice versa in fact grandline  believes that the leader of Sword has to  be either kuzan or fujitora and there  are multiple reasons for this I will  link that video down in the description  because it makes some great points now  of course we know that fujitora dislikes  the world government he has openly  disobeyed them before and he even  orchestrated the destruction of the  warlord system seemingly without  clearance from up above that said  fujitora is believed to have joined the  Marines only two years ago and sword  must have been around for longer than  that so what about kuzan could he be a  secret double agent and the shadow  commander of Sword I mean it's certainly  possible since we know that kuzan has  been an influential Marine for decades  we know that the Ohara incident upset  him and changed him as a person and we  know that he is clearly willing to defy  the will 