of the world government he  chose to spare the lives of both Robin  and Saul at Great risk to himself and he  even tried to challenge sakazuki for the  position of Fleet Admiral in fact we  know that kuzan was the more popular  choice for Fleet Admiral among the rank  and file Navy officers so that again  speaks to the immense influence that he  has within the organization we also know  that kuzan's original motto wasn't  actually lazy Justice initially his  model was burning Justice which suggests  the opposite of a lazy and laid-back  attitude towards Justice however over  time kuzan's perspective changed  probably after he became disillusioned  with the world government and its  actions especially in light of the  Buster call on O'Hara and so as we are  led to believe after seeing that the  world government and people like  sakazuki have a completely different  understanding of Justice from his own  kuzan concluded that Justice was  relative and he decided to take a  laid-back and lazy approach to it but  this could all be just a facade that has  been expertly perpetuated by kuzan over  the course of many years what if koozan  didn't really change his approach to  Justice what if he decided to secretly  pursue burning Justice while putting up  a lazy front in order to avoid unwanted  attention from the world government so  while publicly kuzan pretended to be  laid back secretly he established sword  and continued to pursue his true vision  of burning Justice through his special  secret organization eventually when  sword was already established and  functioning on its own kuzan decided to  go undercover and Infiltrate The the  Blackbeard Pirates why exactly he did  this is still not known to us but it  could all be a part of his master plan  after all the Blackbeard Pirate just  kidnapped our boy Colby who is a  confirmed member of Sword so we are  likely about to see a face-to-face  encounter between kuzan and Kobe this  would be the perfect opportunity for Oda  to reveal that kuzan is secretly  affiliated with sword and that he and  Kobe are actually on the same side so  I'll be watching closely for that  encounter personally I do like this  Theory because there is something  clearly going on with kuza he obviously  has strong moral values and he  disapproves of blatantly unjust acts  like the destruction of wahara he is  also willing to openly defy the world  government by sparing the lives of  individuals like Robin and Saul  individuals who the world government  wanted eliminated at all costs and yet  after clearly showing himself to be a  moral and principled Guy kuzan just  decides to join the most amoral crew in  all of One Piece that definitely doesn't  make sense unless this is all a part of  some secret infiltration scheme but  although I think that kuzan is  definitely affiliated with sword in some  way we can't say for sure that he  himself is the leader or the only leader  that's because we still can't rule out  other influential members of the Old  Guard such as GARP and sengoku in his  video Grand line kind of dismisses the  possibility that GARP or sengoku could  be the leaders behind sword because they  are old and practically retired at this  point I will have to disagree here  because I think there is a lot more yet  to be revealed about these guys their  character arcs are not yet complete and  one or both of them could be behind  sword first let's talk about sengoku  because he actually has a direct  connection to the most important member  of sword that we know to date X Drake we  know that sengoku took in Don Quixote  rosinante when he was still a child and  raised him as his own son rosinante then  Rose to the rank of marine commander and  sengoku tasked him with spying on the  Don Quixote Pirates Who were led by his  older brother doflamingo but what a lot  of people don't seem to know and what we  learned thanks to some Vira card  information is that after he escaped  from his pirate father X Drake was found  by sengoku himself and taken in by the  Marines Drake eventually Rose to the  rank of rear Admiral before going  undercover to spy on the Beast pirates  in a very similar way that rosinante  went to infiltrate the Don Quixote  Pirates now multiple online sources  including the official one-piece Wiki  state that X Drake was taken in by  sengoku and raised as his son in exactly  the same way that rosinante was while  this is possible it is not technically  confirmed I checked with our tour from  the library of O'Hara website and  YouTube channel and he explained that  sengoku found the Drake picked him up  and assigned him to Marine headquarters  but the alleged father-son relationship  is not confirmed not even on the Weaver  cards I mean it could be a father-son  relationship but we have to acknowledge  that we don't have that official  confirmation even though some sources  have claimed that we already do oh and  definitely check out Arthur's Channel he  is incredibly knowledgeable about every  little detail of One Piece Link in the  description so considering the fact that  there is clearly a direct connection  between sengoku and Drake and  considering that the two of them have  known each other ever since Drake first  joined the Marines we certainly can't  rule out that sengoku may be affiliated  with sword this becomes even more  blatantly obvious if the two of them  really did have a father-son  relationship like sengoku and rosinante  and then Drake just happens to end up  with an undercover pirate Mission very  similar to the one that rosinante was  assigned to by sengoku himself if that  father-son relationship is ever  confirmed it will be almost impossible  to imagine that sengoku isn't the one  behind sword or at least that he has  isn't one of its leaders after all  sengoku's dislike for the world  government is well known he nominated  kuzan to become Fleet Admiral over  sakazuki and in general he has become  more and more disillusioned 